THE ORACLE: wasmtime 49.0.3 (f96eabaa1 2026-10-14), .oracle/wasmtime-49.0.3/wasmtime, never the wasmtime on PATH.
build.sh writes its reading to ../p3http.reading: each row is `wasmtime run -S http p3http.wasm <row> <port>
<closed-port>` against peer/ on 127.0.0.1, and the denied row is `get` with no -S http, which fails to link. 10 of 10
runs of every row gave the same stdout, stderr and exit code, which build.sh checks byte for byte before it writes the
reading. No row needs a DNS server: the one name looked up is a `.invalid` one, which never resolves.
